# interplay_lifetime_held_texture_deleted: A normal texture (type 2, private) over guest texels, filled blue by the GPU, then read; a second read waits on the gate while the worker deletes (37) the texture. Released, the texture is made again from its guest page, so the read shows the guest's texels: the fill is lost, unless the fill's exec listed the texture with invalidateGuest and synchronize (6), which wrote it back to the page and so into the new texture. The same in every setup: textures are host copies in the service too.
